cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mathguard in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "mathguard: verify mathematical claims and grade answers against a reference"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: C0MaE
    website: "https://github.com/C0MaE"
abstract: >-
  mathguard checks mathematical claims made by people and language models with
  SymPy and Pint: identities, derivations, calculus, solutions and physical units.
  It finds the faulty step in worked solutions written in Markdown/LaTeX and grades
  final results against a reference, comparing formulas symbolically and numbers
  with unit conversion and a rounding-aware tolerance.
version: 0.3.3
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/C0MaE/mathguard"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/mathguard/"
keywords:
  - verification
  - computer algebra
  - dimensional analysis
  - physics education
  - LLM evaluation
  - sympy
